<title>JAPAN: Japan '96 crude imports down 1.3 pct yr/yr -- MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan '96 crude imports down 1.3 pct yr/yr -- MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's crude oil imports in 1996 totalled 263.5 million kilolitres (kl), down 1.3 percent from 266.9 million kl the previous year, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Imports from the Middle East accounted for 80 percent of the total imports, against 78.6 percent a year earlier.</p>
<p>In 1996, Japanese refiners processed 243.7 million kl of crude against 242.9 million kl the previous year.</p>
</text>
